-- title:
--   Flat cotangent bound for level raising at an auxiliary prime
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a complete discrete valuation ring (a domain, discretely valued, complete for its maximal-adic topology) and let $\bar\rho$ be a two-dimensional residual Galois representation over the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$. Let $p\neq q$ be primes with $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$, and let $S,U$ be finite sets of naturals with $p\in S$, $q\notin S$ and $U\subseteq S$. For a complete noetherian local $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $A$, consider the deformation condition on a rank-two adically continuous representation $\rho$ over $A$ asserting: the determinant is cyclotomic at $p$, $\rho$ is flat at $p$, $\rho$ is unramified at every prime outside the allowed set, and for every $r\in U$ prime with $r\neq p$ the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ is $(X-1)^2$ for every $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup at every place over $r$. Let $D_0$ be a universal deformation datum for $\bar\rho$ with allowed set $S$ and $D'$ one with allowed set $S\cup\{q\}$ (so each carries an absolutely irreducible $\bar\rho$, a universal ring $R$ with residue field generated by the image of $\mathcal{O}$, a representation of the stated type with residual representation equivalent to the base change of $\bar\rho$, and the universal property). Let $\theta\colon R'\to R_0$ and $x_0\colon R_0\to\mathcal{O}$ be local $\mathcal{O}$-algebra maps, with $\theta$ surjective and the base change of the universal representation of $R'$ along $\theta$ equivalent to that of $R_0$. Let $P$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $P$, let $\sigma$ be a $\mathbb{Q}$-automorphism of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $P$ and acting on the residue field of $P$ by $x\mapsto x^q$, and assume every valuation subring with $q$ a non-unit is a Galois conjugate of $P$. Let $a\in\mathcal{O}$ be such that the characteristic polynomial of $\sigma$ acting on the base change of the representation of $D_0$ along $x_0$ is $X^2-aX+q$. Then the $\mathcal{O}$-length of the cotangent module $I/I^2$ of $I=\ker(x_0\circ\theta)$ is at most the $\mathcal{O}$-length of the cotangent module of $\ker x_0$ plus the $\mathcal{O}$-length of $\mathcal{O}/\big((q-1)(a^2-(q+1)^2)\big)$.
--
--   This is the flat-deformation form of Wiles' bound comparing the tangent-space (here cotangent) invariants of two universal deformation rings whose allowed ramification sets differ by one auxiliary prime $q$, the error term being measured by $(q-1)(a^2-(q+1)^2)$ for the Frobenius trace $a$ at $q$. It is used in the construction of the patching data for the Hecke-algebra side, in the three [`CuspForm.heckeLocal`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) statements that cite it.
